    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0791" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1947v01/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.40/8–3047</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Counselor of the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bohlen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lovett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1947-09-02">September 2, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have made a very brief account of our meeting at the War Department on
                        Saturday,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d391-f1"/> and I suggest that it be held in
                    your safe. If you agree I might orally convey the substance of the meeting to
                    Mr. Hickerson,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d391-f2"/> Mr. Rusk,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d391-f3"/> and Mr. Wood<anchor n="4" xml:id="d391-f4"/> and of
                    course to Mr. Armour,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d391-f5"/> Mr. Kennan and Mr.
                        Henderson<anchor n="6" xml:id="d391-f6"/> when they return. I suggest no
                    distribution of the memorandum in the Department in order to insure against any
                    possibility of a leak.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Bohlen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d391-a1.xml" xpointer="d391-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d391-a2.xml" xpointer="d391-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d391-f1" n="1" xml:id="d391-f1-content">
                <p>August 30.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f2" n="2" xml:id="d391-f2-content">
                <p>John D. Hickerson, Director of the Office of European Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f3" n="3" xml:id="d391-f3-content">
                <p>Dean Rusk, Director of the Office of Special Political Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f4" n="4" xml:id="d391-f4-content">
                <p>Presumably C. Tyler Wood, Deputy to the Assistant Secretary of State for Economic
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f5" n="5" xml:id="d391-f5-content">
                <p>Norman Armour, Assistant Secretary of State for Political Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d391-f6" n="6" xml:id="d391-f6-content">
                <p>Loy W. Henderson, Director of the Office of Near Eastern and African Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
